---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works — SENTINEL MAN"
  description="Four engines. One intelligence system. The Brief Engine, Decision Engine, Pattern Engine, and Debrief Engine — each with a distinct job, all drawing from the same operational data."
  ogTitle="How SENTINEL MAN Works — Four Engines, One Voice"
  ogDescription="Four AI engines working from your daily data: morning brief, 5-lane decision analysis with failure-mode forecast, pattern detection, weekly debrief. See exactly how the system operates."
  twitterTitle="How SENTINEL MAN Works — Four Engines, One Voice"
  twitterDescription="Four AI engines working from your daily data. Morning brief, 5-lane decision analysis with failure-mode forecast, pattern detection, weekly debrief."
>
  <div class="content-wrap">
    <div class="content-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">THE ARCHITECTURE</div>
      <h1>Four engines.<br /><strong>One intelligence system.</strong></h1>
      <p class="lead">SENTINEL MAN is not a single AI responding to prompts. It is a coordinated system — four specialised engines working from your data to produce intelligence that improves the longer you use it.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="mini-engines">
        <div class="mini-engine"><div class="num">01</div><div class="name">Brief Engine</div></div>
        <div class="mini-engine"><div class="num">02</div><div class="name">Decision Engine</div></div>
        <div class="mini-engine"><div class="num">03</div><div class="name">Pattern Engine</div></div>
        <div class="mini-engine"><div class="num">04</div><div class="name">Debrief Engine</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="split-text" style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto">
        <p>Each engine has a distinct job. Each draws from the same data store — your check-ins, your decisions, your Operating Principles — and produces a different form of intelligence. None of them work in isolation. Together they build a model of how you operate that no single AI session can produce.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">ENGINE 01 — DAILY</div>
      <h2>The <strong>Brief Engine.</strong></h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split-text">
          <p>Every morning, before you open your inbox, SENTINEL MAN produces your operational brief. Not a generic motivational message. A data-driven intelligence report, specific to your state on that specific day.</p>
          <p>The brief begins with your mode assignment — <strong>COMMAND</strong>, <strong>RECON</strong>, or <strong>STANDBY</strong> — determined by the system from your check-in data and recent trend. Your mode sets the tone for everything that follows. A COMMAND mode brief is aggressive and directive. A RECON brief is observational, diagnostic. STANDBY is minimal — the system knows today is not the day to push hard.</p>
          <p>Below the mode: your Readiness Score (0–100), your decision quality window (the hours your data says your judgment is sharpest), and three operational levers — specific, actionable moves for that day. No generic advice. Each lever is derived from the pattern the system has built about you.</p>
          <p>Above the daily call sits your <strong>weekly objective</strong> — one headline objective per Monday-week that you set on COCKPIT. SENTINEL reads it back to you every morning until it is done or you mark it breached. One call per week. Not a list. The discipline is forcing one call.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="phone-frame" style="margin:0 auto;width:280px">
          <div class="phone-notch"><div class="notch-bar"></div></div>
          <div class="phone-screen">
            <div class="p-datestamp">THU 08 MAY — 06:34 AEST</div>
            <div class="p-mode">▶ COMMAND MODE</div>
            <div class="p-readiness">84</div>
            <div class="p-score-label">READINESS SCORE — PERSONAL BASELINE</div>
            <div class="p-rule"></div>
            <div class="p-brief">Sleep debt: 8 minutes. HRV elevated. Cognitive load: optimal. Your peak decision window opens at 06:34 and closes at approximately 12:00. Three levers identified.</div>
            <div class="p-rule"></div>
            <div class="p-lever"><span class="p-lm">▸</span><span class="p-lt">Front-load decisions before 11am</span><span class="p-tag">↑ DECISION</span></div>
            <div class="p-lever"><span class="p-lm">▸</span><span class="p-lt">Physical output before first business action</span><span class="p-tag">↑ CLARITY</span></div>
            <div class="p-lever"><span class="p-lm">▸</span><span class="p-lt">Contact M. — 21 days elapsed</span><span class="p-tag">◈ NETWORK</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="phone-home"><div class="home-bar"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHAT FEEDS THE BRIEF ENGINE</div>
      <h2>The <strong>daily check-in.</strong></h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="mock-card">
          <div class="mock-label">DAILY CHECK-IN — UNDER 90 SECONDS</div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">MOOD VECTOR</div><div class="mock-body">Fog · Edged · Flat · <strong style="color:var(--gold)">[Solid]</strong> · Apex</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">SLEEP HOURS</div><div class="mock-body">7h <span style="opacity:0.4">▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯</span></div></div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">PHYSICAL LOAD</div><div class="mock-body"><strong style="color:var(--gold)">[Rested]</strong> · Loaded · Crushed</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">MENTAL CLARITY</div><div class="mock-body">4 / 5 <span style="opacity:0.4">▮▮▮▮▯</span></div></div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">NETWORK PULSE</div><div class="mock-body">Degraded · <strong style="color:var(--gold)">[Stable]</strong> · Optimal</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">CARRY-FORWARD (OPTIONAL)</div><div class="mock-body">Board deck review before 1600 →</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="split-text">
          <p>Five inputs. Under 90 seconds. No typing unless you choose to. The check-in is deliberately minimal — because a tool you do not use daily produces no intelligence at all.</p>
          <p>The five inputs — mood vector, sleep hours, physical load, mental clarity, and network pulse — feed directly into your Readiness Score calculation. A sixth optional field, <strong>carry-forward</strong>, lets you log an open item in under ten words. That item appears in tomorrow's brief until you clear it.</p>
          <p>From Day 7 onward, your scores are calculated against your personal baseline — not population averages. A Readiness Score of 71 means something different for you than for the man next to you. The system learns the difference.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">ENGINE 02 — ON DEMAND</div>
      <h2>The <strong>Decision Engine.</strong></h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split-text">
          <p>When you face a significant decision, you submit it to the Decision Engine. Five AI models analyse it in parallel — each with a different mandate. Within 26 seconds, a synthesised assessment arrives. One voice. Five perspectives already resolved, with a failure-mode forecast attached.</p>
          <p><strong>The Reasoner</strong> — checks the decision against your history and your Operating Principles. Has this pattern appeared before? What did your data look like on days you made similar choices?</p>
          <p><strong>The Contrarian</strong> — attacks the obvious choice. What are the specific kill shots? What is the worst-case outcome? What are you not seeing because you are inside the decision?</p>
          <p><strong>The Context Enhancer</strong> — finds the variables you are not considering. Second and third-order consequences. Relational ripples. What happens to the people adjacent to this decision?</p>
          <p><strong>The Predictor</strong> — estimates what you will actually do. Based on your behaviour patterns, are you genuinely evaluating this — or have you already decided and are seeking validation?</p>
          <p><strong>The Pre-mortem</strong> — forecasts the most likely 90-day failure mode for this specific decision and names the early-warning signal that would tell you it's failing in time to course-correct, plus the one guardrail worth attaching before you commit.</p>
          <p>Every assessment ships with a <strong>calibration disclosure</strong>: a collapsible card showing exactly what data the council was reasoning from — your operator record counts, the cohort archetype matched, which lanes ran with which models. Trust by disclosure, not by claim.</p>
          <p>Every assessment ends with a <strong>SOVEREIGNTY CHECK</strong> — a question, not an answer. The council informs. You decide. Always. A 42-year-old founder with 15 years of building his own judgment doesn't want a system that tells him what to do; he wants one that sharpens his own call.</p>
          <p>The Decision Engine is capped at <strong>7 calls per day</strong>. The cap is not a limitation — it's a discipline mechanic. You decide which decisions deserve the full council. That selection process — naming what's actually significant before submitting — is itself part of the product.</p>
          <p>The council is not your echo chamber. From Day 1, before any personal pattern data exists, the lanes draw from <strong>1,600 simulated decisions across 8 archetypes</strong> matched to your profile. The Contrarian runs on a different model architecture with no access to your principles. External reference is built in.</p>
          <p>Every call you log outcomes against makes the next call sharper. After 50 logged outcomes the Reasoner knows your hit rate by decision type (people decisions: 58% right call; financial: 81%), which conditions correlate with your best and worst calls, and which lane was most predictive for your specific patterns. <strong>The council gets smarter at your flavour of decisions over time.</strong> That's compounding intelligence — the most important long-term value the product produces.</p>
          <p>Decision Engine ships with three modes:</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid var(--gold)"><strong>COUNCIL</strong> — full five-lane assessment described above. 7 per day. For decisions where 26 seconds of analysis earns its keep.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid var(--blue)"><strong>FAST</strong> — sub-5-second Haiku response. One risk flag, one question. 10 per day. For live negotiations, board meetings in progress, deals closing on the phone — when council time is too long.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid var(--muted)"><strong>REPLAY</strong> — submit a past decision plus what actually happened. The council retroactively assesses what it would have said at the time. 5 per day. Best for decisions you got wrong — empirical proof that gut + council beats gut alone.</p>
          <p>Every council assessment also surfaces:</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Black-swan tail risks</strong> from the Pre-mortem lane — 1–2 low-probability high-impact scenarios with the early signal that would tell you they're activating.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Multi-OP conflict resolution</strong> — when two of your active principles fight each other on a decision (e.g. <em>"move fast"</em> vs <em>"72-hour buffer"</em>), the system names the tension and hands the resolution back to you. The most valuable decision-coaching the system produces.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Alliance Risk Forecast</strong> — when the decision text mentions a contact in your network, the Context Enhancer adds a probability estimate of relational damage over the next 90 days, with the specific dynamic named.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-card">
          <div class="mock-label">DECISION ASSESSMENT — 26 SECONDS</div>
          <div class="mock-row gold"><div class="mock-lane">REASONER</div><div class="mock-body">Identical structure to April hiring decision. OP 1 conflict detected. Third path available — 14-day compressed trial.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row red"><div class="mock-lane">CONTRARIAN</div><div class="mock-body">$180K with no trial period. If this fails, the referring client absorbs reputational damage. You are being pressured by your own calendar.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row blue"><div class="mock-lane">CONTEXT</div><div class="mock-body">Your best client is the referral source. A failure here doesn't only affect the contract — it implicates that relationship.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row purple"><div class="mock-lane">PREDICTOR</div><div class="mock-body">You are seeking permission for an exception you have already committed to internally — not genuinely deciding.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-row" style="border-left:2px solid var(--gold)"><div class="mock-lane">PRE-MORTEM</div><div class="mock-body">Most likely failure: trial structure waived, scope creep by Week 3.<br />Early warning: client extending requirements before Week 2 deliverable lands.<br />Guardrail: written scope cap before signature, revisit only with formal change order.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-synthesis"><div class="mock-lane">◈ SOVEREIGNTY CHECK</div><div class="mock-body">If this offer arrived with a 60-day start and standard trial structure — would you take it? That question isolates the opportunity from the pressure.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">ENGINE 03 — LONGITUDINAL</div>
      <h2>The <strong>Pattern Engine.</strong></h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="mock-card">
          <div class="mock-label">PATTERN LEDGER — ACTIVE SIGNALS</div>
          <div class="mock-row gold"><div class="mock-lane">SLEEP-DECISION CORRELATION</div><div class="mock-body">Decision quality drops 31% when sleep debt exceeds 45 min. Pattern consistent across 14 data points.<br /><span style="color:var(--gold);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em">CONFIDENCE: HIGH · 14 DATA POINTS</span></div></div>
          <div class="mock-row blue"><div class="mock-lane">AFTERNOON REACTIVE DECISIONS</div><div class="mock-body">Decisions made after 3pm on high-load days are 40% more reactive than baseline.<br /><span style="color:var(--blue);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em">CONFIDENCE: MEDIUM · 8 DATA POINTS</span></div></div>
          <div class="mock-row" style="border-left:2px solid var(--muted)"><div class="mock-lane" style="color:var(--muted)">NETWORK-CREATIVITY LINK</div><div class="mock-body">Strong social contact weeks correlate with higher clarity scores 2 days later.<br /><span style="color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em">CONFIDENCE: EMERGING · 5 DATA POINTS</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="split-text">
          <p>Most tools show you how you felt today. SENTINEL MAN builds a model of how you operate over time — detecting the correlations that repeat in your data before you are consciously aware of them.</p>
          <p>The Pattern Engine runs two scans. A daily light scan checks for emerging signals — possible correlations in your most recent data. It never surfaces a pattern until the evidence threshold is met. A weekly deep scan runs a full analysis across your history, confirming patterns, updating confidence scores, and retiring patterns that no longer hold.</p>
          <p>The patterns that matter most are the ones that reveal your <strong>decision conditions</strong> — the physiological and situational states that predict your best and worst calls. "Decision quality drops 31% when sleep debt exceeds 45 minutes and physical load is high." That is not a population statistic. That is your data.</p>
          <p>The Pattern Engine also produces three operator-facing outputs you can act on directly:</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Cohort Percentile</strong> — your decision-quality and readiness benchmarked against the synthetic operator cohort matched to your archetype (founder under cash stress, executive in transition, late-career professional, etc.). Percentile rank, mode-mix comparison, plus one top-decile gap tactic. Activates with 10+ rated decisions or 14+ daily logs.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Network Activation</strong> — when your contacts list shows overdue people, SENTINEL generates 1–3 short outreach drafts prioritised by leverage to your weekly objective, with a recommended channel. Operator-voice, ready to copy-edit-send. 3 generations per day.</p>
          <p style="padding-left:14px"><strong>Dynamic Principle Refactoring</strong> — every 7 days at most, SENTINEL reads your decision outcomes and proposes ≤3 changes to your Operating Principles (additions, edits, retirements). Each cites specific decisions as evidence. You accept what fits. Reject what doesn't. The system never edits your principles for you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">ENGINE 04 — WEEKLY · QUARTERLY · ANNUAL</div>
      <h2>The <strong>Debrief Engine.</strong></h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split-text">
          <p>Every Sunday evening, the Debrief Engine synthesises your week. Not a mood summary. A performance review — the kind a serious athlete would review between training sessions.</p>
          <p>The debrief covers what changed, what degraded, what improved, what your decision quality looked like, and which Operating Principle was tested during the week. It closes with your primary objective for the next cycle — a single actionable focus that carries forward automatically to Monday's brief.</p>
          <p>The arc continues beyond the week. On the last day of every calendar quarter, <strong>THE SIGNAL</strong> fires — a 280–400 word digest of what crystallised, what is drifting, and what the next quarter demands. After reading THE SIGNAL, you know whether the trajectory of the last 90 days is the trajectory you intended. At Day 365, the <strong>Annual Review</strong> closes the year-long arc with a five-section verdict on the operator you have become.</p>
          <p>The DEBRIEF tab is searchable. Every brief — weekly, milestone, quarterly, annual — has clickable section anchors and a master/detail reader on desktop. Search across the full archive with hit highlighting. By Week 12 your debriefs are an intelligence record on yourself. The reader is built to treat them that way.</p>
          <p>Your <strong>Performance Ledger</strong> is exportable as a credentialed, dated, call-sign-stamped record. A founder going into a Series A. An executive going into a board review. A consultant pitching a new engagement. <em>"Here is my decision record for the last 18 months — what I was right about, what I was wrong about, what the pattern shows."</em> No other product produces this.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-card">
          <div class="mock-label">WEEKLY DEBRIEF — WEEK 7</div>
          <div class="mock-row"><div class="mock-lane">PERFORMANCE SUMMARY</div><div class="mock-body">
            Decision quality: <strong style="color:var(--gold)">74%</strong> <span style="opacity:0.4">▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯</span><br />
            Readiness trend: <strong style="color:var(--green)">+6%</strong> vs Week 6 <span style="opacity:0.4">▮▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯▯</span><br />
            Network health: <strong style="color:var(--text)">Stable</strong>
          </div></div>
          <div class="mock-row gold"><div class="mock-lane">PRINCIPLE TESTED THIS WEEK</div><div class="mock-body">OP 2: No hire decision without 72-hour cooling period. Two opportunities arose. Protocol held on one. The second was borderline — flagged for review.</div></div>
          <div class="mock-synthesis"><div class="mock-lane">◈ NEXT CYCLE OBJECTIVE</div><div class="mock-body">Reduce reactive decisions after 3pm — implement end-of-day decision cutoff protocol before Week 8.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">THE COMPOUND</div>
      <h2>Your model of yourself <strong>lives here.</strong></h2>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:16px;max-width:760px">
        Every check-in, every decision, every principle edit, every weekly debrief feeds the same long memory. After 180 days of use the system holds a confirmed pattern library of how you operate, a decision history of every significant call you've made with outcomes attached, the lifecycle of every principle you've created or retired, and a calibration baseline tuned to your specific archetype.
      </p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:760px">
        The longer you use it, the more expensive it becomes to leave. That's not a threat — it's the value. <strong>No competitor can give you back six months of your own data.</strong>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">THE DISTINCTION</div>
      <h2>Not what you have <strong>tried before.</strong></h2>
      <p class="section-sub" style="text-align:left;margin:0 0 16px">Every tool claims to be different. Here is the specific difference.</p>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="compare-col">
          <div class="compare-head">OTHER PLATFORMS</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Generic population data applied to your situation</li>
            <li>Mood tracking with no decision intelligence layer</li>
            <li>Single AI giving one perspective on every decision</li>
            <li>Employer-purchased — your manager knows you use it</li>
            <li>Wellness language designed for a different audience</li>
            <li>Insights that reset every session, no longitudinal model</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-col win">
          <div class="compare-head">SENTINEL MAN</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Your personal baseline builds from Day 1. Every score is yours.</li>
            <li>Five AI lanes analyse every decision — including the contrarian kill shots and a pre-mortem failure-mode forecast</li>
            <li>Pattern intelligence that accumulates across 90 days and beyond</li>
            <li>Man-sovereign. You buy it. Nobody at HR knows. Your data.</li>
            <li>Performance language — the system speaks the way you think</li>
            <li>Operating Principles gate — every decision checked against your own values</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <FinalCTA
    heading="See it working"
    headingStrong="on your data."
    sub="Seven days. No credit card."
    subLine2="The system starts building from Day 1."
    cta="Begin your 7-day trial →"
  />
</BaseLayout>
